From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:52:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: Program a channel's overlay window from all its
 layers

A channel blends up to four layers in its overlay window before its
scaler; layer 3 is on top. Give the visible layers of a channel the
slots in zpos order, place each in the window by its source-pixel
offset, set the window, scaler and CSC from the union of the layers,
and blend them pre-multiplied, as the BSP does for mixed channels.

Reject what one window cannot show: layers of a channel not adjacent in
z, different scale factors, fractional sources, offsets between source
pixels, different YUV formats or encodings, YUV off the chroma grid,
AFBC and an active colour pipeline. Planes of a CRTC all join a commit,
as one layer moves the slots of the others.

No channel has more than one plane yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
